  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.30.53 - AM032 conditional-access null-handling precision\n\n            Changed:\n            - Hardened AM032 so conditional access only suppresses nullable-source converter diagnostics when it actually handles the null path. Unsafe invocation/constructor arguments such as DateTime.Parse(source?.Trim()), int.Parse(source?.Trim()), DateTime.Parse(trimmed), new Uri(source?.Trim()), or target-typed new(source?.Trim()) in Uri converters, null-forgiven ?? null! fallbacks, coalesced guards whose null fallback enters unsafe branches, maybe-null local member dereferences, and nested-helper-only null checks now report.\n            - Preserved safe AM032 suppression for TryParse success/fallback flows, boolean guard locals, source-free fallback assignments, split-assigned conditional-access locals, nullable parse provider/style arguments, null-tolerant argument targets, boolean switch-statement fallback flows, nullable-destination fallback local returns, and other guarded conditional-access flow shapes while rejecting guards that run after unsafe source dereferences.\n\n            Validation:\n            - Focused AM030/AM032/AM033 slice passing on net10.0 (121 tests)\n            - Full solution test suite passing on net10.0 (985 tests)\n            - Rule catalog and sample diagnostics snapshot checks passing\n            - Analyzer and test projects build clean under -warnaserror (the release gate)\n\n            Previous Release: v2.30.52 - AM006/AM004 aggregate + nested code-fix actions",
